.LONG TERM...
Issued at 118 AM PDT Wed Aug 12 2026
(Thursday through Tuesday)

Cooling and moistening trend continues through Friday as global
ensemble clusters are in agreement that upper-level troughing will
remain over the West Coast. By the weekend, heights will begin to
rise as upper-level ridging builds in from the Southeast while
simultaneously a cutoff low develops off the Pacific Northwest.
Sensible weather wise, this will result in a gradual warming trend
and an increase in onshore flow; however, temperatures will remain
below normal.

