.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 525 AM PDT Wed Aug 12 2026

The marine layer is at roughly 1500-2000ft this morning, but the
view from satellite is currently blocked due to high clouds moving
in. Expect the stratus to hold where it is at, with minimal
expansion into the South and East Bay valleys. Elsewhere, MVFR to IFR
cigs are being observed where there is stratus with the exception
being KSTS where cigs are LIFR. Look for conditions to improve by
mid to late morning, with high clouds lingering. Tonight, the
stratus is expected to return. There`s a curve ball as an upper low
and an additional disturbance move through. Will this keep the
stratus at hand, allow it to expand or will the pattern shift up a
bit with the high cloud? Opted to keep the pessimistic forecast of
stratus returning tonight and into tomorrow morning, but this will
need to be monitored. Moderate to high confidence in the forecast
through Wednesday evening. Moderate confidence for Wednesday evening
into Thursday morning.

Vicinity of SFO...Stratus detections is a bit difficult this morning
due to the high clouds overhead. Looking at webcams and stations
around the San Francisco Bay, there are some MVFR cigs present.
Current thinking is we should stay VFR with only a FEW or SCT MVFR
cigs possible through mid to late morning. High clouds linger into
the afternoon with the next challenge being winds. Some guidance
keeps SSW to SW through the day, while others try to bring onshore
winds back. May need to adjust the winds by the 15Z update if the
trend continues for SW this afternoon. Tonight, guidance tries to
bring back stratus, but confidence is too low to sock us in with low
clouds.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Another cloudy start to the morning, as
stratus seeped into the terminals early Tuesday evening. Look for
conditions to clear by mid to late morning, retreating to the coast.
Models show an afternoon of VFR conditions, but it will dependent on
on just how far back the stratus pulls. Tonight, expect it to return
early on with Thursday morning potentially being interesting. An
upper level disturbance swings just to our north, which could bring
some drizzle to the terminals. This hasn`t been added to the
forecast due to timing issues if this were to happen.


