.MARINE...
(Today through Monday)
Issued at 525 AM PDT Wed Aug 12 2026

Fresh to strong northwest winds will continue into early Thursday
with for the northern outer waters. Isolated near gale gusts will
continue through Wednesday morning. Seas will be rough and  around
9 to 11 feet, with wave heights slowly subsiding through Thursday.
Long period southerly swell will gradually increase  late in the
week, peaking between 16 to 18 seconds late Friday  through early
Sunday. Expect haze and smoke to limit visibility at times along
the Big Sur coast due to the Timber fire.

