.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 118 AM PDT Wed Aug 12 2026

Near-critical fire weather conditions Wednesday afternoon through
Thursday early morning across Monterey and San Benito Counties due
to high based thunderstorms. Confidence remains low for a low
probability/high impact scenario of elevated rain
showers/thunderstorms across the Central Coast from a low pressure
system that is currently 300 miles southwest of Point Conception.
Erratic/gusty outflow winds of 35-45 mph can be expected with any
elevated rain showers/thunderstorms. Lightning will pose the risk
for new fire starts and has the potential to hinder operations on
the Timber Fire in Big Sur. The areas of most concern will be in the
higher terrain above the marine layer (1,500 feet), namely the Santa
Lucia Mountains and Gabilan Range. Poor minimum daytime relative
humidity around 30% is expected in the afternoons with little-to-no
recovery overnight.

